Group By
----------
	- Group By clause is used to divide similar data items into set of logical groups 
	- group by clause automatically reduces number of rows in ach group 
	- This group by clause is in select statement 

	syntax:
		select columnname,.....
		from tablename
		group by columnname;

Q: write a query to display number of employees in each departments by using group by clause 
	
		================================	
		SQL> select deptno,count(*)
		  2  from emp
		  3  group by deptno;

		    DEPTNO   COUNT(*)
		---------- ----------
		        30          6
		        10          3
		        20          5

		SQL>
		======================================

Q: write a query to display number of employees in each job in emp table by using group by clause 
	
		=========================			
		SQL> select job,count(*)
		  2  from emp
		  3  group by job;

		JOB         COUNT(*)
		--------- ----------
		CLERK              4
		SALESMAN           4
		ANALYST            2
		MANAGER            3
		PRESIDENT          1

		SQL>
		===========================

Q: write a query to display minimum and maximum salary from each departments from emp table by using group by clause 
		
		======================================
		SQL> select deptno,min(sal),max(sal)
		  2  from emp
		  3  group by deptno;

		    DEPTNO   MIN(SAL)   MAX(SAL)
		---------- ---------- ----------
		        30        950       2850
		        10       1300       5000
		        20        800       3000
		SQL>
		===================================

Note1:In all Relational databases we can also use group by clause without using group Functios also

	Example:
		======================		
		SQL> select deptno
		  2  from emp
		  3  group by deptno;

		    DEPTNO
		----------
		        30
		        10
		        20

		SQL>
		==========================


Rule: Here in group by concept after select statement we specify normal column and group functions columns and Those Normal columns must be specify after group by clause also, If not specifying normal columns after group by clause then oracle DB will return an error


SQL> SELECT DEPTNO,SAL
  2  FROM EMP
  3  GROUP BY DEPTNO;
SELECT DEPTNO,SAL
              *
ERROR at line 1:
ORA-00979: not a GROUP BY expression

	-> from above error because we specify two normal columns after select command then after we only specify single column only thats why its shows error   
	-> How many normal columns we specify after select command those many normal columns should be after group by clause  


	Example-1:
		===========================
		SQL> SELECT DEPTNO,SAL
		  2  FROM EMP
		  3  GROUP BY DEPTNO,SAL;

		    DEPTNO        SAL
		---------- ----------
		        30       1250
		        20       2975
		        30       2850
		        20       3000
		        10       1300
		        10       5000
		        30        950
		        20        800
		        30       1500
		        20       1100
		        30       1600
		        10       2450

		12 rows selected.

		SQL>
		====================================

	Example-2:
		===================================	
		SQL> SELECT DEPTNO,JOB,SUM(SAL)
		  2  FROM EMP
		  3  GROUP BY DEPTNO,JOB;

		    DEPTNO JOB         SUM(SAL)
		---------- --------- ----------
		        20 MANAGER         2975
		        20 ANALYST         6000
		        10 PRESIDENT       5000
		        10 CLERK           1300
		        30 SALESMAN        5600
		        10 MANAGER         2450
		        20 CLERK           1900
		        30 MANAGER         2850
		        30 CLERK            950

		9 rows selected.

		SQL>
		=========================================================

	-> observe above columns those columns must be in left to right specified in group by clause 



Group by Clause Excution:
--------------------------
	- Whenever we are using or submitting group by clause into Oracle server first it will process select specified columns from group by clause and then only it returns 
	- similarly data items into set of groups from that column and also automatically reduces number of rows in each group and this result is internally stord in result table. then only oracle server retrive select list specified columns from this result set table 

	Example:
		===============================================		
		SQL> SELECT DEPTNO FROM EMP GROUP BY DEPTNO;

		    DEPTNO
		----------
		        30
		        10
		        20

		SQL>
		==================================================

		